      {
        "id": 163055,
        "name": "Yak Guardian",
        "username": "Yak_Guardian",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/yak_guardian/{size}/1884_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-20T07:26:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"skoticus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/skoticus/48/1964_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> skoticus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Yak Guardian wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;ChronoRanger_101 wrote:<br><blockquote>I wonder if the Ennead might be allies that can come to our aid from the mission decks? And maybe that's why he didn't come out and say yes or know.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nThat's pretty much how I interpreted it as well. Well, Off to BGG to make a Anubis &amp; the Heroic Ennead deck. &nbsp; :wink: \n</blockquote></div>\nI already did! Several months ago! And then someone else (don't remember their name now) put the cards together. Go ahead and check it out!&nbsp;<a href=\"https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/1316847/villain-hero-conversion-ennead\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/1316847/villain-hero-conversion-ennead</a>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Since there might be a delay in the arrival of playtesting material (for a perfectly reasonable reason), I'll run these through my test script and post the results over in the BGG thread. &nbsp;Thanks!</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
